---
description: Query Standards and SQL Formatting
globs: ["**/*.pp"]
alwaysApply: true
---

When writing queries:

1. Query Naming:
- Must match the associated detection name exactly
- Use lowercase with underscores

2. SQL Structure Template:
```hcl
query "service_event_name" {
  sql = <<-EOQ
    select
      ${local.detection_sql_resource_column_request_parameters_name}
    from
      aws_cloudtrail_log
    where
      event_source = 'service.amazonaws.com'
      and event_name = 'SpecificEvent'
      ${local.detection_sql_where_conditions}
    order by
      event_time desc;
  EOQ

  tags = local.service_common_tags
}
```

3. SQL Formatting Rules:
- Use 2-space indentation
- Write keywords in lowercase
- Place one condition per line
- Always use <<-EOQ heredoc syntax
- Include order by event_time desc
- Use consistent column aliases
- Add comments for non-obvious conditions using --
